From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] nx2: after an ASTC decode image finds no memory, no new one is asked for for 8-64 frames (waveydude's 0923, EDEN_NX2_ASTC_DECODE_BACKOFF), off by default

What: an ASTC texture is decoded on the GPU into a temporary RGBA8 storage image (TranscodeAstcToBcn,
and TranscodeAstcBatched with EDEN_UP_ASTC_BATCH_MIB). When memory is short every ASTC texture the
frame meets asks the allocator for its own decode image; each ask that fails is a VMA attempt and a
driver refusal and, with EDEN_NX2_TRANSCODE_WAIT=1, an upload that goes back for later anyway. At an area load under 0 MiB
free that is dozens of failed requests a frame on the GPU thread.

With EDEN_NX2_ASTC_DECODE_BACKOFF=1 (exact "1", read once): after a new decode image is refused
(none made, or with TRANSCODE_WAIT an unbacked one), no new decode image is asked for until 8, 16,
32, then 64 frames have passed (the n-th refusal in a row waits 2^min(n+2,6) frames). Meanwhile an
upload that needs a new one is refused as TRANSCODE_WAIT refuses it (upload_refused: the image stays
CPU-modified and is tried again at its next use; with 0664's EDEN_NX2_UPLOAD_BACKOFF that use waits
too). A decode image of the same shape that is free for reuse is still taken. One made resets the
count. A Render_Vulkan warning at the 1st, 2nd, 4th, 8th ... refusal in a row.

Use it with EDEN_NX2_TRANSCODE_WAIT=1 (our env has it). Without it an upload held back here
is still refused and redone later; it is never drawn from an empty decode.

Changed from his: the switch (his patch has none: always on); his NoteAstcDecodeStorageRefusal /
Success are one NoteAstcDecodeStorage(bool); his "upload_refused = true" inside the refusal note is
left where the code already sets it; the frame counter is runtime_frame (his runtime_frame_index);
his min(.., 64) is dropped (the shift already stops at 64).

Off: one u64 increment per frame (runtime_frame, unconditional, read only by the switch), one test
of a static bool per new decode image (none for a reused one); no wait, no line. Not in the
kept-store stamp.

Origin and credit: waveydude, ocarina-private patch 0923 ("Back off repeated ASTC decode storage
allocation failures"), commit 6001e12.

T153 integration review: NoteAstcDecodeStorage is noexcept and runs exactly when memory was
refused; its LOG_WARNING formats a std::string, so a std::bad_alloc there would end the process.
The line is now wrapped in a std::bad_alloc catch (a line that finds no memory is left out).
---
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.cpp
index a17273b..e207555 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.cpp
@@ -3358,6 +3358,7 @@ void TextureCacheRuntime::ReleaseMsaaScratchImage(VkImage image) {
 }
 
 void TextureCacheRuntime::TickFrame() {
+    ++runtime_frame;
     static constexpr u32 MAX_UNUSED_SCRATCH_FRAMES = 60;
     LogTrim2d();
     // EDEN_NX2_CLEAN_BY_TIME=1: the unused-frame counters below (decode images, copy buffers, MSAA
@@ -5546,6 +5547,41 @@ void TextureCacheRuntime::AccelerateImageUploadLayers(
     astc_decoder_pass->AssembleLayers(image, map, swizzles, layers);
 }
 
+namespace {
+[[nodiscard]] bool AstcDecodeBackoff() {
+    static const bool enabled = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_NX2_ASTC_DECODE_BACKOFF");
+    return enabled;
+}
+} // Anonymous namespace
+
+bool TextureCacheRuntime::AstcDecodeStorageHeldBack() const noexcept {
+    return AstcDecodeBackoff() && runtime_frame < astc_decode_retry_frame;
+}
+
+void TextureCacheRuntime::NoteAstcDecodeStorage(bool made) noexcept {
+    if (!AstcDecodeBackoff()) {
+        return;
+    }
+    if (made) {
+        astc_decode_fail_count = 0;
+        astc_decode_retry_frame = 0;
+        return;
+    }
+    ++astc_decode_fail_count;
+    const u64 backoff_frames = u64{1} << (std::min<u32>)(astc_decode_fail_count + 2, 6);
+    astc_decode_retry_frame = runtime_frame + backoff_frames;
+    if ((astc_decode_fail_count & (astc_decode_fail_count - 1)) == 0) {
+        // noexcept, and memory is short here: a line that finds none is left out.
+        try {
+            LOG_WARNING(Render_Vulkan,
+                        "EDEN_NX2_ASTC_DECODE_BACKOFF: an ASTC decode image found no memory ({} "
+                        "times in a row): no new one for {} frames",
+                        astc_decode_fail_count, backoff_frames);
+        } catch (const std::bad_alloc&) {
+        }
+    }
+}
+
 void TextureCacheRuntime::TranscodeAstcToBcn(
     Image& image, const StagingBufferRef& map,
     std::span<const VideoCommon::SwizzleParameters> swizzles) {
@@ -5643,6 +5679,10 @@ void TextureCacheRuntime::TranscodeAstcToBcn(
         pending = std::move(*reusable);
         free_transcodes.erase(reusable);
     } else {
+        if (AstcDecodeStorageHeldBack()) {
+            upload_refused = true;
+            return;
+        }
         // With no memory the allocator gives an image with nothing bound (or, with no room for
         // that either, throws).
         vk::Image decode_image;
@@ -5670,9 +5710,11 @@ void TextureCacheRuntime::TranscodeAstcToBcn(
             }
         }
         if (!decode_image || (wait_for_memory && decode_image.IsUnbacked())) {
+            NoteAstcDecodeStorage(false);
             upload_refused = true;
             return;
         }
+        NoteAstcDecodeStorage(true);
         pending = PendingTranscode{
             .tick = 0,
             .image = std::move(decode_image),
@@ -5822,12 +5864,18 @@ void TextureCacheRuntime::TranscodeAstcBatched(
         scratch = std::move(*reusable);
         free_transcodes.erase(reusable);
     } else {
+        if (AstcDecodeStorageHeldBack()) {
+            upload_refused = true;
+            return;
+        }
         vk::Image scratch_image = make_decode_image(plan.scratch_width, plan.scratch_height,
                                                     plan.scratch_levels, plan.scratch_layers);
         if (!scratch_image || (wait_for_memory && scratch_image.IsUnbacked())) {
+            NoteAstcDecodeStorage(false);
             upload_refused = true;
             return;
         }
+        NoteAstcDecodeStorage(true);
         scratch = PendingTranscode{
             .tick = 0,
             .image = std::move(scratch_image),
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.h b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.h
index 66c6928..b887404 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.h
@@ -336,6 +336,18 @@ public:
     /// See TakeUploadRefused.
     bool upload_refused = false;
 
+    /// EDEN_NX2_ASTC_DECODE_BACKOFF=1 (exact "1"; waveydude's 0923): after a decode image for an
+    /// ASTC texture found no memory, no new one is asked for until runtime_frame passes
+    /// astc_decode_retry_frame (8, 16, 32, then 64 frames after the n-th refusal in a row); the
+    /// upload is refused as TRANSCODE_WAIT refuses it and tried again at the image's next use. A
+    /// decode image that is made resets the count. Off: never read or written but runtime_frame.
+    u64 runtime_frame = 0;
+    u64 astc_decode_retry_frame = 0;
+    u32 astc_decode_fail_count = 0;
+
+    [[nodiscard]] bool AstcDecodeStorageHeldBack() const noexcept;
+    void NoteAstcDecodeStorage(bool made) noexcept;
+
     /// Temporary decode images, reusable once the GPU is past `tick`.
     struct PendingTranscode {
         u64 tick;
